url: /en/tutorial/6-islands/\n  - heading \"Sponsored by\" [level=2]\n  - link \"Netlify\":\n    - /url: https://www.netlify.com/?utm_campaign=Astro-2024&utm_source=astro-referral\n  - link \"Webflow\":\n    - /url: https://webflow.com/feature/cloud?utm_source=Astro&utm_medium=tech-partner&utm_campaign=fy26-astro&utm_content=fy26-docs\n  - link \"Cloudflare\":\n    - /url: https://www.cloudflare.com/?utm_source=astro&utm_medium=astro&utm_campaign=astro\n  - link \"Mux\":\n    - /url: https://www.mux.com/?utm_campaign=21819274-Astro&utm_source=astro\n  - link \"Image Kit\":\n    - /url: https://imagekit.io/?utm_source=astro&utm_medium=astro&utm_campaign=astro\n  - link \"Mintlify\":\n    - /url: https://www.mintlify.com/?utm_source=astro&utm_medium=astro&utm_campaign=astro\n- complementary:\n  - navigation \"Tutorial Tracker\":\n    - heading \"Tutorial Tracker\" [level=2]\n    - tablist:\n      - tab \"Unit 0 (0/2 Complete)\"\n      - tab \"Unit 1 (0/6 Complete)\" [selected]\n      - tab \"Unit 2 (0/6 Complete)\"\n      - tab \"Unit 3 (0/5 Complete)\"\n      - tab \"Unit 4 (0/4 Complete)\"\n      - tab \"Unit 5 (0/5 Complete)\"\n      - tab \"Unit 6 (0/5 Complete)\"\n    - tabpanel \"Unit 1 (0/6 Complete)\":\n      - heading \"Create and deploy your first Astro site\" [level=2]\n      - list:\n        - listitem:\n          - 'link \"To-do 0 Check in: Unit 1 - Setup\"':\n            - /url: /en/tutorial/1-setup/\n        - listitem:\n          - link \"To-do 1 Prepare your dev environment\":\n            - /url: /en/tutorial/1-setup/1/\n          - list:\n            - listitem:\n              - link \"Get the dev tools you need\":\n                - /url: \"#get-the-dev-tools-you-need\"\n            - listitem:\n              - link \"Checklist for moving on\":\n                - /url: \"#checklist-for-moving-on\"\n        - listitem:\n          - link \"To-do 2 Create your first Astro project\":\n            - /url: /en/tutorial/1-setup/2/\n        - listitem:\n          - link \"To-do 3 Write your first line of Astro\":\n            - /url: /en/tutorial/1-setup/3/\n        - listitem:\n          - link \"To-do 4 Store your repository online\":\n            - /url: /en/tutorial/1-setup/4/\n        - listitem:\n          - link \"To-do 5 Deploy your site to the web\":\n            - /url: /en/tutorial/1-setup/5/\n  - complementary \"Learn Astro with James Q Quick\":\n    - img \"Scrimba\"\n    - heading \"Learn Astro with James Q Quick\" [level=2]:\n      - strong: Learn Astro\n      - text: with James Q Quick\n    - paragraph: Build your first site with 35 interactive Scrimba lessons\n    - link \"Get 20% off\":\n      - /url: https://scrimba.com/intro-to-astro-c00ar0fi5u?via=astro\n- main:\n  - heading \"Prepare your dev environment\" [level=1]\n  - paragraph: Get ready to\u2026\n  - list:\n    - listitem: Install any tools that you will use to build your Astro website\n  - heading \"Get the dev tools you need\" [level=2]\n  - link \"Section titled \u201cGet the dev tools you need\u201d\":\n    - /url: \"#get-the-dev-tools-you-need\"\n  - heading \"Terminal\" [level=3]\n  - link \"Section titled \u201cTerminal\u201d\":\n    - /url: \"#terminal\"\n  - paragraph:\n    - text: You will use a\n    - strong: command line (terminal)\n    - text: to create your Astro project and to run key commands to build, develop, and test your site.\n  - paragraph:\n    - text: You can access the command line through a local terminal program for your operating system. Common applications include\n    - strong: Terminal\n    - text: (MacOS/Linux),\n    - strong: Command Prompt\n    - text: (Windows), and\n    - strong: Termux\n    - text: (Android). One of these will probably already be on your machine.\n  - heading \"Node.js\" [level=3]\n  - link \"Section titled \u201cNode.js\u201d\":\n    - /url: \"#nodejs\"\n  - paragraph:\n    - text: For Astro to run on your system, you will also need to have a compatible version of\n    - link \"Node.js\":\n      - /url: https://nodejs.org/en/\n      - strong: Node.js\n    - text: installed. Astro supports\n    - strong: even-numbered\n    - text: Node.js versions. The current minimum supported version is\n    - code: v22.12.0\n    - text: . Odd-numbered versions like\n    - code: v23\n    - text: are not supported.\n  - paragraph: \"To check to see whether you already have a compatible version installed, run the following command in your terminal:\"\n  - figure \"Terminal window\":\n    - text: Terminal window\n    - code: node -v // Example output v22.20.0\n    - button \"Copy to clipboard\"\n  - paragraph: If the command returns a version number supported by Astro, you\u2019re good to go!\n  - paragraph:\n    - text: If the command returns an error message like\n    - code: Command 'node' not found\n    - text: \", or a version number lower than the required, then you need to\"\n    - link \"install a compatible Node.js version\":\n      - /url: https://docs.npmjs.com/downloading-and-installing-node-js-and-npm\n    - text: .\n  - heading \"Code Editor\" [level=3]\n  - link \"Section titled \u201cCode Editor\u201d\":\n    - /url: \"#code-editor\"\n  - paragraph:\n    - text: Additionally, you will need to download and install a\n    - strong: code editor\n    - text: to write your code.\n  - paragraph:\n    - text: \"We\u2019ll use\u2026: This tutorial will use\"\n    - strong: VS Code\n    - text: \", but you can use any editor for your operating system.\"\n  - paragraph: Complete the following steps in order.\n  - paragraph:\n    - text: First,\n    - link \"Download and install VS Code\":\n      - /url: https://code.visualstudio.com/#alt-downloads\n    - text: or another code editor of your choice.\n  - heading \"Test your knowledge\" [level=3]\n  - link \"Section titled \u201cTest your knowledge\u201d\":\n    - /url: \"#test-your-knowledge\"\n  - paragraph: Which of the following is\u2026\n  - list:\n    - listitem:\n      - paragraph: A code editor, for making changes to your files and their content?\n      - list:\n        - listitem:\n          - radio \"web browser\"\n          - paragraph: web browser\n        - listitem:\n          - radio \"Terminal\"\n          - paragraph: Terminal\n        - listitem:\n          - radio \"VS Code\"\n          - paragraph: VS Code\n      - button \"Submit\" [disabled]\n      - alert\n    - listitem:\n      - paragraph: An online version control provider for your repository?\n      - list:\n        - listitem:\n          - radio \"GitHub\"\n          - paragraph: GitHub\n        - listitem:\n          - radio \"Terminal\"\n          - paragraph: Terminal\n        - listitem:\n          - radio \"VS Code\"\n          - paragraph: VS Code\n      - button \"Submit\" [disabled]\n      - alert\n    - listitem:\n      - paragraph: An application for running commands?\n      - list:\n        - listitem:\n          - radio \"GitHub\"\n          - paragraph: GitHub\n        - listitem:\n          - radio \"Terminal\"\n          - paragraph: Terminal\n        - listitem:\n          - radio \"web browser\"\n          - paragraph: web browser\n      - button \"Submit\" [disabled]\n      - alert\n  - heading \"Checklist for moving on\" [level=2]\n  - link \"Section titled \u201cChecklist for moving on\u201d\":\n    - /url: \"#checklist-for-moving-on\"\n  - list:\n    - listitem:\n      - checkbox \"I can access the command line in a terminal.\"\n      - text: I can access the command line in a terminal.\n    - listitem:\n      - checkbox \"I have Node.js installed.\"\n      - text: I have Node.js installed.\n    - listitem:\n      - checkbox \"I have a code editor like VS Code.\"\n      - text: I have a code editor like VS Code.\n  - heading \"Resources\" [level=3]\n  - link \"Section titled \u201cResources\u201d\":\n    - /url: \"#resources\"\n  - list:\n    - listitem:\n      - paragraph:\n        - link \"FreeCodeCamp.org\":\n          - /url: https://freecodecamp.org\n        - text: external \u2014 a free educational site with full courses or quick refreshers in HTML, CSS, JS, and more.\n  - link \"Edit page\":\n    - /url: https://github.com/withastro/docs/edit/main/src/content/docs/en/tutorial/1-setup/1.mdx\n  - link \"Translate this page\":\n    - /url: https://contribute.docs.astro.build/guides/i18n/\n  - 'link \"Previous Check in: Unit 1 - Setup\"':\n    - /url: /en/tutorial/1-setup/\n  - link \"Next Create your first Astro project\":\n    - /url: /en/tutorial/1-setup/2/\n  - link \"Contribute\":\n    - /url: /en/contribute/\n  - link \"Community\":\n    - /url: https://astro.build/chat\n    - img\n    - text: Community\n  - link \"Sponsor\":\n    - /url: https://opencollective.com/astrodotbuild"